From: Thomas Gleixner <tglx@linutronix.de>
Date: Tue, 9 Mar 2021 09:42:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 135/327] tasklets: Use spin wait in tasklet_disable()
 temporarily
Origin: https://git.kernel.org/cgit/linux/kernel/git/rt/linux-stable-rt.git/commit?id=a7c24eaf1dd65a8b335a72f99d46208d4661b700

To ease the transition use spin waiting in tasklet_disable() until all
usage sites from atomic context have been cleaned up.

Signed-off-by: Thomas Gleixner <tglx@linutronix.de>
Signed-off-by: Sebastian Andrzej Siewior <bigeasy@linutronix.de>
---
 include/linux/interrupt.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/interrupt.h b/include/linux/interrupt.h
index dd0db52f192a..96299f508d9b 100644
--- a/include/linux/interrupt.h
+++ b/include/linux/interrupt.h
@@ -756,7 +756,8 @@ static inline void tasklet_disable_in_atomic(struct tasklet_struct *t)
 static inline void tasklet_disable(struct tasklet_struct *t)
 {
 	tasklet_disable_nosync(t);
-	tasklet_unlock_wait(t);
+	/* Spin wait until all atomic users are converted */
+	tasklet_unlock_spin_wait(t);
 	smp_mb();
 }
 
